  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Clinique Vétérinaire des Jasmins, at 714 avenue Rhin et Danube in Vence, welcomes dogs, cats and small exotic pets in a setting equipped with recent technology (digital X-ray, ultrasound, full blood analysers), with CCTV in the hospitalisation area and a digital health record that can be viewed online. The website also offers an online shop and a customer account to fill in your dog's e-health record. The clinic does not advertise an on-site emergency service at night.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The clinic is open Monday to Saturday (Monday-Friday 8:30am-12pm and 2:30pm-7pm, Saturday 9am-12:30pm and 2:30pm-6pm, closed on Sunday). The website specifies that Dr Diana Jasmin-Rigault and her colleague see patients by appointment, which can be booked online (on CaptainVet or on the clinic's website) or by calling 04 93 58 39 72. Outside opening hours, the website asks you to call this same number 24/7: the call is redirected to an on-call vet.</p>
      <p>The practice is in Vence, on the road to Tourrettes-sur-Loup. The team has two vets and two veterinary nursing assistants. Private car parks and a space for people with reduced mobility are in front of the door, which makes arriving with a dog on a leash or an animal to carry easier. The technical facilities include digital X-ray, ultrasound and full blood analysers, with a surveillance camera in the hospitalisation area. The website also lets you order food and non-prescription products, to be collected at the clinic the next day.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: save the clinic's number in your phone as soon as you arrive in Vence, it can come in handy if something unexpected comes up.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The old town of Vence, perched in the hinterland above Nice, is a few minutes from the clinic. The road to Tourrettes-sur-Loup leads to neighbouring villages for a walk with your dog, to be done respecting each town's leash rules.</p>
